WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:11.770
- What kind of questions
can science not currently answer

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:13.770
and may never be able to answer?

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:14.603
- Yeah...

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.250
Is there intelligence out there

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.190
that underlies the whole thing?

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:23.571
You can call him with the
"G" word, if you want.

00:00:23.571 --> 00:00:28.571
I can say, are we a computer
simulation with a purpose?

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.500
Is there an agent, an intelligent agent

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:39.120
that underlies, or is
responsible, for the whole thing?

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.510
Does that intelligent agent
satisfy the laws of physics?

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.540
Does it satisfy the laws
of quantum mechanics?

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.360
Is it made of atoms and molecules?

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.460
Yeah, there's a lot of questions.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:52.993
And I don't see, it seems
to me, a real question.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:55.420
- [Lex] It's an
answerable question--

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:56.700
- Well, I don't know if it's answerable.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.263
The questions have to be
answerable to be real.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:04.130
Some philosophers would
say that a question

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.433
is not a question unless it's answerable.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.220
This question doesn't
seem to me answerable

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:12.273
by any known method,

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.403
but it seems to me real.

